##:
net/error -- NetError, the error vocabulary of the net modules.

`NetError` is a predefined enum: the compiler synthesizes it, and this module is its
HOME (#574). The import is what brings the bare name into a unit, as `<io/fs>` brings
`FileMode`, and `use <net/error> as ne` puts it behind the dot (`ne.NetError.TimedOut`).
Every net module answers it -- `connect`, `bind`, `resolve`, `parse_ip` -- so a unit that
matches on one of their errors imports this module beside the one it calls.

The variant ORDER is the ABI: the index is the tag the socket layer stores into a Result
payload, so a variant is only ever appended.
:##
